---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../styles/pixlfit.css';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — PixelFit">
	<div class="page-layout">
		<main class="legal-shell">
			<a href="/" class="legal-back">← Back to PixlFit</a>
			<article class="legal-doc">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="legal-effective"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 1, 2026</p>
				<p>
					Welcome to PixelFit (&quot;we&quot;, &quot;our&quot;, or &quot;us&quot;). Your privacy is important to us.
				</p>

				<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
				<p>We aim to collect as little data as possible. Depending on how you use the site, we may collect:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Usage Data:</strong> Basic information such as browser type, device type, and pages visited.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Analytics Data:</strong> We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google tag / gtag.js) to see
						aggregate traffic and how pages are used. Google receives data such as pages viewed, device/browser type,
						and general location (e.g. region). See
						<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google&apos;s Privacy Policy</a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Uploaded Images:</strong> Images you upload are processed locally in your browser and are not
						stored on our servers.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
				<p>We use collected information to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Improve website performance and user experience</li>
					<li>Understand usage trends</li>
					<li>Maintain security and prevent abuse</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. Image Processing</h2>
				<p>
					All image processing (cropping, resizing, filtering) occurs locally in your browser whenever possible.
				</p>
				<p>We do not upload, store, or retain your images on our servers.</p>

				<h2>4. Cookies</h2>
				<p>Google Analytics may set cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) or use similar storage to recognize returning visits
					and measure traffic. You can use your browser&apos;s cookie controls, opt-out browser add-ons, or
					Google&apos;s tools described in their policy to limit this data.</p>

				<h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
				<p>
					We may use third-party services (such as analytics providers) that collect limited information in
					accordance with their own privacy policies.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Data Security</h2>
				<p>
					We take reasonable measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission over the
					internet is 100% secure.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Children&apos;s Privacy</h2>
				<p>
					This service is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from
					children.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised
					effective date.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Contact</h2>
				<p>If you have any questions, you can contact us at:</p>
				<p>
					<a href="mailto:perennialwebstudio@gmail.com">perennialwebstudio@gmail.com</a>
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</div>
</Layout>
